Wet-path alignment: does Amount move the vocal in time?
  Gated 220 Hz burst; arrival measured as the first crossing of 20%
  of the burst's steady RMS. Lag is wet arrival MINUS dry arrival.

  amount                               lag(smp)      lag(ms)
  ----------------------------------   --------  -----------
  reported latency: 2885 samples (60.10 ms)

  Amount 1                                  -69       -1.44
  Amount 25                                 -69       -1.44
  Amount 50                                 -69       -1.44
  Amount 100                                -69       -1.44

  worst wet-vs-dry shift: 69 samples (1.44 ms)
  This is how far the vocal jumps when Amount leaves zero. It is
  invisible to --nulltest, which only ever sees the dry delay line.
